# Assistant API (I11, spec 04 "Assistant"). Run the AppHost (or the API) with a chat model: LM Studio, or
# AI:ActiveChatProfile = openrouter with a key in user secrets. VS Code REST Client / Rider / Visual Studio keep the
# owner cookie (fs_sid) between requests, so the conversation stays yours.
# With curl: curl -kN -c jar.txt -b jar.txt ... --data-binary @message.json (a UTF-8 file for Cyrillic text).

@api = https://localhost:7180

### Start a conversation (body optional; locale = movie texts when a request has no Accept-Language)
# @name conversation
POST {{api}}/api/chat/conversations
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: ru

{ "locale": "ru" }

### Send a message: the answer streams as server-sent events
# message.started → tool.started → tool.completed → movies → message.delta… → message.completed (or error)
POST {{api}}/api/chat/conversations/{{conversation.response.body.id}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: ru

{ "text": "Посоветуй что-нибудь про космос" }

### Continue the conversation (filters come from the text: no horror, at most $5)
POST {{api}}/api/chat/conversations/{{conversation.response.body.id}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: ru

{ "text": "А что-нибудь из этого без ужасов и подешевле, до 5 долларов?" }

### Reload: user messages and answers with movie cards (current prices), usage and cost
GET {{api}}/api/chat/conversations/{{conversation.response.body.id}}
Accept-Language: ru

### The owner's conversations
GET {{api}}/api/chat/conversations

### Swedish
# @name svConversation
POST {{api}}/api/chat/conversations
Accept-Language: sv

###
POST {{api}}/api/chat/conversations/{{svConversation.response.body.id}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: sv

{ "text": "Tipsa om en film om rymden" }

### Rate an answer (messageId from message.started / message.completed)
POST {{api}}/api/chat/messages/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/feedback
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rating": 1, "comment": "good picks" }
